| `DEEPINFRA_API_URL` | `https://api.deepinfra.com` |
| `DEEPINFRA_INFERENCE_MODEL` | Chat completion model id (build server: `Qwen/Qwen3-32B`) |
| `DEEPINFRA_EMBEDDING_MODEL` | `Qwen/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B` |
| `DEEPINFRA_RERANKER_MODEL` | `Qwen/Qwen3-Reranker-0.6B` |
| `STORAGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` | `https://s3.vtc.com` — server URL rewrite (`storage.mdc`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_STORAGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` | `https://s3.vtc.com` — browser display |
| `VITE_STORAGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` | same — auto-mirrored for static Vite |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_MAP_STYLE_URL` | `https://maps.vtc.com/styles/basic-preview/style.json` |
| `VITE_MAP_STYLE_URL` | same — auto-mirrored for static map apps |
| `MAPTILER_API_KEY` | MapTiler Cloud — mirrored to `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` / `VITE_*` |
| `MAPTILER_STYLE_URL` | `https://api.maptiler.com/maps/streets-v2/style.json?key={key}` — mirrored to browser vars |
| `DEEPINFRA_CHAT_MODEL` | `openai/gpt-oss-120b-Turbo` — fast chat / tool calls (replaced Cerebras) |
| `DEEPINFRA_CHAT_INPUT_PRICE_PER_M` / `DEEPINFRA_CHAT_OUTPUT_PRICE_PER_M` | `0.15` / `0.60` |
| `DEEPINFRA_REASONING_EFFORT` | `low` (gpt-oss) |
| `AI_DEFAULT_PROVIDER` | always `deepinfra` (Groq and Cerebras retired 2026-10-17 — their vars are stripped from builds) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL` | `wss://ws.vtc.com` — browser Socket.IO (`realtime.mdc`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_IO_PATH` | `/socket.io` (default path) |
| `SOCKET_IO_URL` | `(platform-injected internal URL)` — server-side emit from API routes (vRack → server1 relay) |
| `PUBLIC_CHAT_SERVER_URL` | `https://chat.vtc.com` — chat REST API (shell + child apps; `realtime.mdc`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_NETWORK_URL` | `https://app.vtc.com` — shell login + chat deep links (`/dashboard/chat/…`) |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_VTC_URL` | `https://vtc.com` — marketing / “Explore VTC” on unauthenticated landing |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_POSIF_URL` | same — legacy alias injected in parallel |

Unused `DEEPINFRA_*` vars in non-RAG apps are harmless. Realtime, chat, shell, storage, and map style vars are harmless in apps that do not use them.

### Per-app secrets (not global)

| Variable | When |
|----------|------|
| `MONGODB_URI` | **Dedicated** apps (fixed publisher DB). **Shared** apps: publisher / `group=0` fallback only — tenanted silos use SDK `getDb()` + `VTC_API_URL`, not env `MONGODB_URI`. |
| Developer Environment keys | App-specific (e.g. `ZAPI_INTERNAL_SECRET`, custom model overrides) |

### Not injected at app deploy

| Concern | Production path |
|---------|-----------------|
| **Object storage** | `@vtc/sdk/storage` → `GET ${VTC_API_URL}/api/v1/credentials/` → **MinIO** (not `HETZNER_*` / not `MINIO_*` in `.env.production`). **Public `<img>` URLs:** commit `STORAGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` + `NEXT_PUBLIC_STORAGE_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` = `https://s3.vtc.com` — rewrite internal MinIO URLs (`storage.mdc`) |
| **Private npm** | `NPM_VTC_PASSWORD_B64` in `/opt/generate-app/.env` — injected at Docker build (`--build-arg`) and host `npm ci` for `@vtc/*` from `https://npm.vtc.com` — `vtc-packages.mdc` |
| **`VTC_API_URL` / `POSIF_API_URL` / `DEEPINFRA_*` / realtime / chat / shell URLs in git** | Remove from app `.env.production` — platform injects on every build |

Agents: do **not** bulk-edit `VTC_API_URL` across app repos for deploy fixes — change the build service `.env` or redeploy.

## Node version

Match `package.json` engines (`node >=22 <23`) to the platform base image (`node:22-alpine`).

## Platform Docker build (`registry.vtc.com/{app}:…`)

The Dockerfile lives on the **build platform**, not in the app repo. A typical image build:

1. `npm ci` — peer-dependency warnings from `eslint-config-next` vs `eslint@10` are **expected** and non-fatal.
2. **`NPM_VTC_PASSWORD_B64`** — build server injects Verdaccio auth before `npm ci` when the app uses `@vtc/*` (`ensure_vtc_npmrc` in `generate-app`; set in `/opt/generate-app/.env`). Apps commit `.npmrc` with `${NPM_VTC_PASSWORD_B64}` placeholder — never the raw token.
3. Platform writes `MONGODB_URI` into `.env` / `.env.production` for `next build` (secrets are injected at build time).
4. `npm run build` → compile → **Running TypeScript** → static generation.

### `context canceled` is not a TypeScript error

If the log shows `✓ Compiled successfully` then `Running TypeScript ...` then `CANCELED` / `context canceled`, the build was **interrupted** (CI timeout, manual cancel, deploy pipeline abort) — not a type-check failure.

A real TypeScript failure looks like:

```
Failed to compile.
./src/...: Type error: ...
```

**Action:** Re-run the deploy/build. If it cancels repeatedly at the same step, increase build timeout or check build-server load — not app source unless `Failed to compile` appears.

### Next.js 16 — Turbopack vs `webpack` config (common build failure)

**Symptom** (at `npm run build` inside Docker):

```
ERROR: This build is using Turbopack, with a `webpack` config and no `turbopack` config.
```

**Cause:** Apps scaffolded with `dev-watch.mdc` add a dev-only `webpack` hook. Next.js 16 defaults production builds to Turbopack unless told otherwise.

**Fix** (use both — reference `~/apps/jobs`):

1. Add `turbopack: {}` to `next.config.ts` / `.js` next to the `webpack` hook.
2. Set `"build": "next build --webpack"` in `package.json`.

The `webpack` hook only runs `watchOptions` when `dev` is true — it does not affect production bundles. `turbopack: {}` satisfies Next.js 16; `--webpack` ensures Docker uses the same bundler if Turbopack defaults change.

**Verify before push:**

```bash
grep -E 'turbopack|webpack' next.config.*
grep '"build"' package.json
npm run build
```

A follow-on `WorkerError: Call retries were exceeded` is usually the same clash — not a separate Docker issue.

### Harmless Docker warnings

- `FromPlatformFlagConstDisallowed: FROM --platform flag` — platform image template; safe to ignore unless the platform team changes base images.
- `SecretsUsedInArgOrEnv: NPM_VTC_PASSWORD_B64` — expected; build server injects Verdaccio auth via `--build-arg` (`vtc-packages.mdc`).
- `npm audit` / eslint peer warnings during `npm ci` — do not block the image build.

### Env vars the platform must merge at build/runtime

| Variable | Source | When needed |
|----------|--------|-------------|
| `VTC_API_URL`, `POSIF_API_URL`, `DEEPINFRA_*` | Build service `.env` | Every Next.js deploy — overrides repo |
| `MONGODB_URI` | ZAPI per-app | Dedicated apps; shared publisher DB fallback |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_WS_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_SOCKET_IO_PATH`, `SOCKET_IO_URL`, `PUBLIC_CHAT_SERVER_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_NETWORK_URL`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_POSIF_URL` | Build service `.env` | Platform shell / realtime / chat — overrides repo |
| `APP_NAME`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL`, `APP_DEPLOYMENT_TYPE`, `APP_PORT` (if missing) | Build inject (`apply_app_identity_env_vars`) | Identity — overrides stale repo URL/name |
| Other app-specific keys | Committed `.env.production` + Developer Environment | Per `env-development.mdc` |

Document new **app-specific** keys in **`env_development`** (template) and **`.env.production`**. Do not document platform-injected or build-injected identity vars in app repos — see tables in **Build-injected identity** and **Platform constants**.

### Local verification before push

```bash
npm run build
```

Must pass locally. Docker build runs the same `next build` with platform-injected `MONGODB_URI`.

